an10.62:6.21 | S: You should say: ‘Faith.’ | T: (none)
an10.62:6.22 | S: I say that faith is fueled by something, it’s not unfueled. | T: (none)
an10.62:6.23 | S: And what is the fuel for faith? | T: (none)
an10.62:6.24 | S: You should say: ‘Listening to the true teaching.’ | T: (none)
an10.62:6.25 | S: I say that listening to the true teaching is fueled by something, it’s not unfueled. | T: Hearing the good Dhamma, too, I say, has a nutriment; it is not without nutriment.
an10.62:6.26 | S: And what is the fuel for listening to the true teaching? | T: And what is the nutriment for hearing the good Dhamma?
an10.62:6.27 | S: You should say: ‘Associating with true persons.’ | T: It should be said: (10) associating with good persons.
an10.62:7.1 | S: In this way, when the factor of associating with true persons is fulfilled, it fulfills the factor of listening to the true teaching. When the factor of listening to the true teaching is fulfilled, it fulfills the factor of faith … rational application of mind … mindfulness and situational awareness … sense restraint … the three kinds of good conduct … the four kinds of mindfulness meditation … the seven awakening factors. When the seven awakening factors are fulfilled, they fulfill knowledge and freedom. | T: “Thus associating with good persons, becoming full, fills up hearing the good Dhamma…. The seven factors of enlightenment, becoming full, fill up true knowledge and liberation.
an10.62:7.2 | S: That’s the fuel for knowledge and freedom, and that’s how it’s fulfilled. | T: Thus there is nutriment for true knowledge and liberation, and in this way they become full.
an10.62:8.1 | S: It’s like when the heavens rain heavily on a mountain top, and the water flows downhill to fill the hollows, crevices, and creeks. As they become full, they fill up the pools. The pools fill up the lakes, the lakes fill up the streams, and the streams fill up the rivers. And as the rivers become full, they fill up the ocean. | T: “Just as, when it is raining and the rain pours down in thick droplets on a mountain top, the water flows down along the slope … and the rivers, becoming full, fill up the great ocean;
an10.62:8.2 | S: That’s the fuel for the ocean, and that’s how it’s filled up. | T: thus there is nutriment for the great ocean, and in this way it becomes full.
an10.62:8.3 | S: In the same way, when the factor of associating with true persons is fulfilled, it fulfills the factor of listening to the true teaching. When the factor of listening to the true teaching is fulfilled, it fulfills the factor of faith … rational application of mind … mindfulness and situational awareness … sense restraint …the three kinds of good conduct … the four kinds of mindfulness meditation … the seven awakening factors. When the seven awakening factors are fulfilled, they fulfill knowledge and freedom. | T: So too, associating with good persons, becoming full, fills up hearing the good Dhamma…. The seven factors of enlightenment, becoming full, fill up true knowledge and liberation.

